    {
      "text": "Adding a small, optimized amount of Pd to NiFeCoCr narrows the statistical distribution of exchange interactions.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A narrower distribution of exchange interactions produces a more homogeneous magnetic state.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pd-induced narrowing of the exchange-interaction distribution produces a sharper, second-order magnetic phase transition.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A sharper magnetic transition enhances the magnetocaloric response at applied fields below 1 T.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pd addition reduces magnetic hysteresis in NiFeCoCr-based alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Pd addition does not impair rapid heat exchange.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Pd addition preserves the mechanical stability of the alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Pd concentration around 5 at.% is expected to produce a sharper magnetic transition than the 0 at.% Pd baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An optimized Pd concentration may increase the maximum magnetic entropy change by up to 40% relative to the 0 at.% Pd baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An optimized Pd concentration is expected to reduce hysteresis relative to the 0 at.% Pd baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Local magnetic probes should reveal a more homogeneous exchange profile in the optimized Pd-containing alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mossbauer spectroscopy or neutron scattering can quantify or map the proposed distribution of exchange interactions.",
